WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.769
Seinfeld is undoubtedly one of the greatest
and most important TV comedies of all time.

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:09.490
It's been off the air for nearly 20 years,
but millions still watch the reruns every

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.179
day, both in syndication and online.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:17.510
After nine seasons and 180 episodes, plenty
of on-set silliness was left on the cutting

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.510
room floor.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.460
Here are some of the funniest bloopers from
the set of Seinfeld.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.200
Not camera-worthy

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.380
Nothing ever seems to go right for unlucky
loser George Costanza.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.300
It would seem that some of that bad luck rubbed
off on actor Jason Alexander, at least in

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.300
this blooper.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.460
The camera is supposed to follow him off-screen,
but it doesn't …

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.440
"Let me just check.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.440
Excuse me.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.940
Excuse me, there's not a camera on me, and
it really ..."

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.579
Throw about nothing

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:52.690
The main characters of Seinfeld have been
called a lot of things—selfish, misanthropic,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.690
self-absorbed.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.790
They all tend to feed off of each other's
nasty energy, and that's on display in this

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.790
blooper.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:03.570
George, Jerry, and Elaine irritate George's
hospital roommate, so George tosses a cup

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.570
over the partition.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.000
Or at least he tries to …

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.800
"Shut up!"

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:21.060
"Ow ow ow!"

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.539
The way the scene crumbles

00:01:22.539 --> 00:01:27.070
Whether or not a cookie can be made into a
paste and forced into the mouth of an unconscious

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:32.490
man is a debate you'll only find on Seinfeld,
but the insanity was too much for Jerry and

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.760
Julia during this take …

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.100
"Cookies don't liquefy!"

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.660
"Yes they can!

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.420
You can liquefy a cookie!"

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.999
Kramer vs. Kramer

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:46.490
Michael Richards is just naturally funny.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:51.630
The role of Kramer often required him to be
funny with just a look, a gesture, or by just

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.240
plain existing, a challenge he executed a
little too well sometimes, cracking up his

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.029
castmates and ruining the take …

00:01:58.029 --> 00:01:59.420
"I'm sorry!

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.340
I'm sorry!

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.840
I'm sorry, it's just that it's so funny!"

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.700
"Okay, we're rolling."

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.920
"We're f---ed up now, I don't know!"

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.659
No part for you

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:15.300
TV Jerry Seinfeld was a stand-up comedian,
just like the real Jerry Seinfeld.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.599
And like his real-life counterpart, TV Jerry
sought out some supplemental acting work on

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:20.599
occasion.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:24.050
But the fictional Seinfeld was not nearly
as successful as the real deal ...

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.040
"I can't act!

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.160
I don't know what the hum duh helm!

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.260
Because I …"
"See?

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.120
I can't."

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:35.650
Bubbling over

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:41.500
Season 4's "The Bubble Boy" ranks among the
silliest and most memorable Seinfeld episodes.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.360
In one scene, Jerry can't stop himself from
jumping the gun and explaining what a "Bubble

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.360
Boy" is ...

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.360
"A Bubble Boy?"

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.260
"Yes, he lives in a bubble."

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.120
"What's a Bubble Boy?"

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.801
"Well, I think Jerry just explained that."

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.260
"He's a what?"

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.349
"He's a Bubble Boy."

00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:00.370
"A Bubble Boy?"

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.109
"He lives in a bubble.

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:04.440
I'm sorry — my fault, my fault."

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.900
"He's a Bubble Boy.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.460
"A Bubble Boy?"

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.460
"Yes, he lives in a bubble."

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.880
"You schmuck!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.040
Will you wait!"

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.280
George wigs out

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:21.079
After six seasons, the self-consciously bald
George did something about his problem and

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:22.830
got himself a toupee.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.030
His newfound sense of confidence draws new
attention from the opposite sex.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.840
George somehow manages to play it cool, and
then, actor Jason Alexander suffers a George

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.720
Costanza moment …

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.620
Garofalo goof

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:46.819
After countless dates, girlfriends dumped
for petty reasons, and otherwise failed relationships,

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:52.219
it looked like Jerry might have finally found
his match, played by Janeane Garofalo, in

00:03:52.219 --> 00:03:54.480
the seventh season episode "The Invitations"
...

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.939
"I tell ya, we've got tremendous — you've
got a line."

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.460
"Yeah."

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.460
"I'm sorry.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.620
Sorry, I'm kissing Jerry Seinfeld.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.939
I get nervous!"

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.360
"It's good luck to kiss a Jew on Passover."

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.080
"Janeane thinks it's good luck to kiss a Jew
on Passover."

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.159
Thanks for watching!

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:13.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.970
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

